  "title": "2 · Transactions, ACID & Concurrency Problems (Unit 3)",
  "learn": "<h3>Transaction</h3><p>A <b>transaction</b> is a program unit whose execution may change the contents of the database, a logical unit of work that must complete entirely to stay correct. Example: transfer 100 from A (300) to B (400): Read A, A=A-100, Write A, Read B, B=B+100, Write B. Before: 300+400 = 700. After: 200+500 = 700, <b>consistent</b>.</p>\n<h3>ACID</h3><p><b>Atomicity</b>: all or nothing (commit makes changes visible, abort hides them). <b>Consistency</b>: a consistent database stays consistent (sum before = sum after). <b>Isolation</b>: a transaction's actions are hidden from others until it terminates. <b>Durability</b>: once committed, updates are permanent.</p>\n<h3>Why run transactions concurrently?</h3><p>Shorter waiting time and better throughput and resource use. The price is four classic problems:</p>\n<p><b>1. Lost update (W-W):</b> x=100. T1 reads 100, T2 reads 100, T1 writes 110, T2 writes 80: T1's update is overwritten.<br><b>2. Dirty read / temporary update (W-R):</b> T1 writes x=110 then fails, but T2 already read 110 and built on it.<br><b>3. Incorrect summary:</b> T2 sums A and Y while T1 changes Y in between, so the total mixes old and new values.<br><b>4. Unrepeatable read (R-W):</b> T1 reads A=1000, T2 changes A to 3000, T1 reads again and gets 3000.</p>\n<h3>Implementing atomicity and durability</h3><p>The <b>recovery manager</b> does it. The simple <b>shadow-database scheme</b> keeps a <b>db_pointer</b> to the current copy; all updates go to a new copy. <b>Abort</b>: ignore the new copy. <b>Commit</b>: flip the pointer to the new copy. It assumes one transaction at a time and no disk failure, so it does not handle concurrency.</p><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 206\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-th\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"18.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T1</text><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"150\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-th\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"18.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"28\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"44.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R(x) → 100</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"54\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"70.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = x + 10</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"152\" y=\"80\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"96.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R(x) → 100</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"152\" y=\"106\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"122.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = x − 20</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"132\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"148.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">W(x) = 110</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"152\" y=\"158\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"174.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">W(x) = 80</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"150.0\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lost update: x ends at 80, T1's +10 is lost (a serial run gives 90)</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 2: lost update (W-W), initial x = 100</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 180\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-th\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"18.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T1</text><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"150\" y=\"0\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-th\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"18.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"28\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"44.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R(x) → 100</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"2\" y=\"54\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"70.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = x + 10; W(x) = 110</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"152\" y=\"80\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"96.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R(x) → 110 (dirty)</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"152\" y=\"106\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"122.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">x = x + 50; W(x) = 160</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"2\" y=\"132\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" rx=\"5\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"148.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FAIL → rollback</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"150.0\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T2 built 160 on a value that never existed</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 3: dirty read / temporary update (W-R)</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 620 160\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"130\" y=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Before commit / abort</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"65.0\" y=\"60.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">db_pointer</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"20\" y=\"110\" width=\"110\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"75.0\" y=\"132.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">old copy</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"160\" y=\"110\" width=\"110\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"215.0\" y=\"132.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">new copy (updates)</text><line class=\"dg-ln\" x1=\"65\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"65\" y2=\"108\" marker-end=\"url(#ar)\"/><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"470\" y=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\">After commit</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"350\" y=\"40\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"395.0\" y=\"60.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">db_pointer</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"330\" y=\"110\" width=\"110\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"385.0\" y=\"132.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">old copy</text><rect class=\"dg-ok\" x=\"470\" y=\"110\" width=\"110\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"525.0\" y=\"132.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">new copy (current)</text><line class=\"dg-ln\" x1=\"420\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"108\" marker-end=\"url(#ar)\"/></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 4: shadow-database scheme. Abort leaves the pointer alone; commit moves it to the new copy</figcaption></figure>",
